OL,3,GNEWSAGovernment failings allowed Covid
OL,4,A'to spread like wildfire' in care
OL,5,Ahomes, inquiry finds
OL,6,
OL,7,FGovernment failures in care settings
OL,8,Fcreated an environment that allowed
OL,9,FCovid to spread like wildfire, an
OL,10,Fofficial inquiry has said.
OL,12,FThe sixth report from the Covid inquiry
OL,13,Fsaid the care sector appeared to be
OL,14,F"something of an afterthought" in the
OL,15,Fearly stages of the pandemic and there
OL,16,Fwas no "protective ring" put around
OL,17,Fhomes as claimed by ministers at the
OL,18,Ftime.
OL,20,FThere were more than 43,000 recorded
OL,21,Fdeaths involving Covid in care homes
OL,22,Fbetween March 2020 and July 2022.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
